From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not read a sent command on timeout

The vendor's bugfix update (uwe5622-allwinner-bugfix-v6.3.patch in the
old Armbian stack) has this change; the uwe5622 repo base lacks it.

A sent command belongs to the tx path, which frees it after transfer or
when it drops it as expired. The timeout message in
sprdwl_cmd_send_recv() still read mstime from it:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in sprdwl_cmd_send_recv+0xcf4/0xf60 [sprdwl_ng]
  Freed by task 877:
   kfree+0x24c/0x490
   sprdwl_tx_cmd.isra.0+0x3c4/0x600 [sprdwl_ng]
   sprdwl_tx_work_queue+0x14c/0x620 [sprdwl_ng]

Print the copy in g_sprdwl_cmd instead.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c
@@ -617,7 +617,7 @@ int sprdwl_cmd_send_recv(struct sprdwl_p
 		}
 	} else {
 		wl_err("ctx_id:%d cmd: %s[%d] rsp timeout (mstime = %d), num=%d\n",
-		       ctx_id, cmd2str(cmd_id), cmd_id, le32_to_cpu(hdr->mstime),
+		       ctx_id, cmd2str(cmd_id), cmd_id, cmd->mstime,
 		       tx_msg->cmd_send);
 		if (cmd_id == WIFI_CMD_CLOSE) {
 			sprdwl_atcmd_assert(priv, ctx_id, cmd_id, CMD_RSP_TIMEOUT_ERROR);
